160	    /**
161	     * The stored E.164 {@link #telephone} formatted for humans as the country code, a single
162	     * space, then the national digits (the digits after the country code) grouped in threes from
163	     * the left, e.g. {@code "+61412345678"} becomes {@code "+61 412 345 678"}. The country code is
164	     * a single digit for the {@code +1} and {@code +7} zones and two digits otherwise.
